[0m[49m[38;5;10m+     83[0m:[38;5;10m[49m ## Divergence found and fixed
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+     84[0m:[38;5;10m[49m 
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+     85[0m:[38;5;10m[49m Rows E7 (and the E5/E6 allocation *ordering*) initially **failed**. LLVM had
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+     86[0m:[38;5;10m[49m deleted the entire `temp_buffer` allocation from the release `cdylib`, because
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+     87[0m:[38;5;10m[49m the Rust translation stored into `temp_buffer[i]` but then read the value back
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+     88[0m:[38;5;10m[49m from a local instead of from memory, making every store dead. Measured with the
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+     89[0m:[38;5;10m[49m interposer, on `gotomach(4, 7, 0, INT_MAX)` with the 3rd `malloc` forced to fail:
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+     90[0m:[38;5;10m[49m 
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+     91[0m:[38;5;10m[49m ```
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+     92[0m:[38;5;10m[49m C        : RESULT=-4  MALLOCS=3
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+     93[0m:[38;5;10m[49m Rust (before): RESULT=128 MALLOCS=1     <-- wrong code, wrong allocation count
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+     94[0m:[38;5;10m[49m Rust (after) : RESULT=-4  MALLOCS=3
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+     95[0m:[38;5;10m[49m ```
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+     96[0m:[38;5;10m[49m 
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+     97[0m:[38;5;10m[49m Two further branches had been optimised out of the Rust `.so` entirely — the
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+     98[0m:[38;5;10m[49m `-4` path above and the `-5` / `[ERROR] Invalid state status` path (LLVM
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+     99[0m:[38;5;10m[49m constant-folded `check_char_flag(1)` after inlining). The fix, in
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    100[0m:[38;5;10m[49m `src/lib.rs`, was to make the Rust perform the same observable work the
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    101[0m:[38;5;10m[49m unoptimised C does: `write_volatile`/`read_volatile` on `temp_buffer[i]`, and
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    102[0m:[38;5;10m[49m `#[inline(never)]` on the four `static` helpers so their allocations and checks
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    103[0m:[38;5;10m[49m survive. All ten log literals and all three allocations now match the C `.so`.
