[38;5;10mc_src/src/lib.c[0m is a single translation unit exporting four symbols: [38;5;10mgotomach(iterations, seed, mode, threshold)[0m plus the three operation callbacks [38;5;10mprocess_value[0m ([38;5;10m+10[0m), [38;5;10mdouble_value[0m ([38;5;10m*2[0m), [38;5;10mtriple_value[0m ([38;5;10m*3[0m). [38;5;10mgotomach[0m validates both [38;5;10miterations[0m and [38;5;10mseed[0m against [38;5;10m[0, 65535][0m, picks a callback by [38;5;10mmode[0m, allocates a [38;5;10mProcessorState[0m and a scratch buffer, runs an iteration loop that appends values below [38;5;10mthreshold[0m, and returns their sum — or one of [38;5;10m-1[0m…[38;5;10m-6[0m via a [38;5;10mgoto cleanup[0m epilogue.[0m[0m
[0m[0m
[38;5;252m[1m## The divergence I found and fixed[0m[0m
[0m[0m
Only one real bug, and it was invisible to happy-path testing. The Rust release [38;5;10mcdylib[0m was [1mmissing two of the C's three [38;5;10mmalloc[0m calls and two of its ten log branches[22m: the translation stored into [38;5;10mtemp_buffer[i][0m but read the value back from a local register instead of from memory, so every store was dead and LLVM deleted the whole allocation — along with its NULL check and the [38;5;10m-4[0m return. Separately, inlining let LLVM constant-fold [38;5;10mcheck_char_flag(1)[0m, deleting the [38;5;10m-5[0m path.[0m[0m
[0m[0m
Measured through the same runner with the 3rd allocation forced to fail:[0m[0m
[0m[0m
[38;5;10mC            : RESULT=-4  MALLOCS=3
