[0m[0m[0m
[0m[0m
The fix in [38;5;10msrc/lib.rs[0m makes the Rust perform the same observable work the unoptimised C does: [38;5;10mwrite_volatile[0m/[38;5;10mread_volatile[0m on [38;5;10mtemp_buffer[i][0m, and [38;5;10m#[inline(never)][0m on the four [38;5;10mstatic[0m helpers. All ten log literals and all three allocations now match.[0m[0m
[0m[0m
Two [38;5;10mERRORS.md[0m rows ([38;5;10m-5[0m, [38;5;10m-6[0m) are provably unreachable in the C — [38;5;10mstatus[0m is always [38;5;10m1[0m, and [38;5;10mcount <= i < capacity[0m always holds. Those are documented as never-taken branches that must still [3mexist[23m, and a symbol/string test enforces that.[0m[0m
